                        <i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i>
                        <span>A1 Beginners Quick Reference</span>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">Mastering Questions in English</h2>
                    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300 text-sm lg:text-base leading-relaxed">
                        Learn when to use <strong class="text-sky-400">Is</strong> vs <strong class="text-sky-400">Are</strong> for Yes/No questions, and how to combine Wh- words with <strong class="text-indigo-400">Is/Are</strong> or <strong class="text-indigo-400">Do/Does</strong> to get to know people!
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                
                <!-- Rule Card 1: Questions with BE (Yes/No) -->
                <div class="bg-slate-800/80 border border-slate-700/80 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-lg">
                    <div>
                        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                            <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
                                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-sky-500/20 text-sky-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">
                                    9
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">1. Yes / No Questions with BE</h3>
                            </div>
                            <button onclick="speakText('Yes No Questions with Be. Use Is for singular subjects and Are for plural subjects.')" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300 p-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-700/50 hover:bg-slate-700 transition" title="Listen to summary">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-volume-high"></i>
                            </button>
                        </div>

                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-4">
                            Start the question with <strong class="text-sky-400">IS</strong> or <strong class="text-sky-400">ARE</strong> to check facts or identities.
                        </p>

                        <!-- Rule Breakdown Box -->
                        <div class="space-y-3">
                            <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-xl p-3.5">
                                <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-sky-400 mb-1">
                                    <span>IS + Singular Subject (He / She / It / Name)</span>
                                    <button onclick="speakText('Is Mike\'s last name Chu?')" class="hover:text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-low"></i></button>
                                </div>
                                <p class="text-sm text-slate-200">
                                    "<strong>Is</strong> Mike an interior designer?"
                                </p>
                                <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1 italic">Answer: Yes, he is. / No, he isn't.</p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-xl p-3.5">
                                <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-sky-400 mb-1">
                                    <span>ARE + Plural Subject (They / We / You / 2+ People)</span>
                                    <button onclick="speakText('Are Mike and Evan conference participants?')" class="hover:text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-low"></i></button>
                                </div>
                                <p class="text-sm text-slate-200">
                                    "<strong>Are</strong> Evan and Bill friends?"
                                </p>
                                <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1 italic">Answer: Yes, they are. / No, they aren't.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-slate-700/60 text-xs text-slate-400 flex items-center">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb text-amber-400 mr-2"></i>
                        <span>Tip: <strong>Mike's last name</strong> is singular (It) = <strong>Is</strong>.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Rule Card 2: Wh- Questions -->
                <div class="bg-slate-800/80 border border-slate-700/80 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-lg">
                    <div>
                        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                            <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
                                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/20 text-indigo-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg">
                                    10
                                </div>
                                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">2. Wh- Questions (Information)</h3>
                            </div>
                            <button onclick="speakText('Wh Questions. Use What, Where, and Who with Is, Are, or Does.')" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 p-2 rounded-lg bg-slate-700/50 hover:bg-slate-700 transition" title="Listen to summary">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-volume-high"></i>
                            </button>
                        </div>

                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 mb-4">
                            Use Wh- words (<strong class="text-indigo-300">What, Where, Who</strong>) to ask for specific information about people.
                        </p>

                        <!-- Rule Breakdown Box -->
                        <div class="space-y-3">
                            <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-xl p-3.5">
                                <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-indigo-400 mb-1">
                                    <span>Wh- + IS / ARE (For identity, origin, or objects)</span>
                                    <button onclick="speakText('Where is Mike from?')" class="hover:text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-low"></i></button>
                                </div>
                                <p class="text-sm text-slate-200">
                                    "Where <strong>is</strong> Mike from?" / "Who <strong>are</strong> the participants?"
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-700/50 rounded-xl p-3.5">
                                <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-1">
                                    <span>Wh- + DOES (For occupations / actions with verbs)</span>
                                    <button onclick="speakText('What does Rachel do?')" class="hover:text-white"><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-low"></i></button>
                                </div>
                                <p class="text-sm text-slate-200">
                                    "What <strong>does</strong> Rachel do?"
                                </p>
                                <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1 italic">Notice: 'do' is the main action verb here = She is an interior designer.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-slate-700/60 text-xs text-slate-400 flex items-center">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info text-sky-400 mr-2"></i>
                        <span>"What does Rachel do?" = What is her job?</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>

